00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:19.730
so that you can start to
now connect the dots.

00:12:19.731 --> 00:12:22.430
In the worldview that
we have at Microsoft,

00:12:22.431 --> 00:12:23.995
that Satya talked
about which is this

00:12:23.996 --> 00:12:26.665
Intelligent Cloud,
Intelligent Edge.

00:12:26.666 --> 00:12:29.430
We talked about this ability
to connect the dots.

00:12:29.431 --> 00:12:31.585
It's not just
disparate interactions

00:12:31.586 --> 00:12:32.985
with different devices.

00:12:32.986 --> 00:12:37.220
It's a multi-device,
multi-sensory coordinated world.

00:12:37.221 --> 00:12:39.835
That coordination,
that glue is in fact

00:12:39.836 --> 00:12:42.750
that connected fabric
of people, of things,

00:12:42.751 --> 00:12:46.150
of the environments, of the
context that is the glue

00:12:46.151 --> 00:12:48.270
that starts to tie
the different pieces

00:12:48.271 --> 00:12:49.785
together into something coherent.

00:12:49.786 --> 00:12:52.910
I want to now give
some examples of the power

00:12:52.911 --> 00:12:56.090
of these experiences
when you have knowledge.

00:12:56.091 --> 00:12:58.170
This is in fact the thing
that gets us excited

00:12:58.171 --> 00:13:01.400
but again we're at
the early stages of it.

00:13:01.750 --> 00:13:05.435
Nice animation. Let's
go with the Bing.

00:13:05.436 --> 00:13:10.065
Starting with Bing. Clearly,
we have the ability

00:13:10.066 --> 00:13:13.360
to have reasonable and
interesting questions

00:13:13.361 --> 00:13:14.410
around the knowledge graph.

00:13:14.411 --> 00:13:17.095
So, in this case, what's
the size of Switzerland,

00:13:17.096 --> 00:13:18.480
there's the knowledge graph,

00:13:18.481 --> 00:13:20.420
there different nodes,
there different facets.

00:13:20.421 --> 00:13:22.130
Based on that, we can now derive

00:13:22.131 --> 00:13:23.600
the computations to answer that,

00:13:23.601 --> 00:13:25.660
in a much more directed fashion.

00:13:25.661 --> 00:13:29.425
You can imagine this across
a large number of domains.

00:13:29.426 --> 00:13:32.355
But we've also recognized

00:13:32.356 --> 00:13:34.335
that that doesn't capture
all the information.

00:13:34.336 --> 00:13:36.105
That there's still
lots of information

00:13:36.106 --> 00:13:37.860
in the billions and
billions of documents.

00:13:37.861 --> 00:13:40.380
That may not be
explicitly represented.

00:13:40.381 --> 00:13:42.250
So, there's lots of advances

00:13:42.251 --> 00:13:43.994
in machine reading comprehension,

00:13:43.995 --> 00:13:46.085
newer modeling deep Q&amp;A

00:13:46.086 --> 00:13:48.245
and these are things that
we have in Bing and also

00:13:48.246 --> 00:13:50.325
in the Milieu bug as well as

00:13:50.326 --> 00:13:54.290
many academia and research
systems that are out there.

00:13:54.291 --> 00:13:57.550
Now we understand
semantically model,

00:13:57.551 --> 00:14:00.875
the knowledge is within snippets,

00:14:00.876 --> 00:14:03.660
different documents,
warranties and

00:14:03.661 --> 00:14:05.765
be able to now have
Q&amp;A around it.

00:14:05.766 --> 00:14:07.875
In fact, we've taken it
one step further and say,

00:14:07.876 --> 00:14:09.095
it's not just one answer and in

00:14:09.096 --> 00:14:10.690
fact there are
different perspectives,

00:14:10.691 --> 00:14:13.085
because when you start
looking at information,

00:14:13.086 --> 00:14:16.100
it is not the facts
only, it is opinions,

00:14:16.101 --> 00:14:18.420
it's perspectives and
the ability to surface

00:14:18.421 --> 00:14:20.845
that and to recognize that
there is also critical.

00:14:20.846 --> 00:14:23.205
So, we have this
multi-perspective answers.

00:14:23.206 --> 00:14:25.855
These are just
examples that now go

00:14:25.856 --> 00:14:29.015
beyond the ranking of
the template links to now

00:14:29.016 --> 00:14:31.770
understanding what is
the inherent intent

00:14:31.771 --> 00:14:33.365
and the need that

00:14:33.366 --> 00:14:35.550
people may have and
how do we start

00:14:35.551 --> 00:14:37.975
to surface that knowledge
is within the web.

00:14:37.976 --> 00:14:39.620
A lot of that requires us to now

00:14:39.621 --> 00:14:41.760
invest in technologies
that now to

00:14:41.761 --> 00:14:43.980
elevate and goes beyond
the indexing the

00:14:43.981 --> 00:14:46.235
posting list and to
start to look at

00:14:46.236 --> 00:14:48.120
the organization of information

00:14:48.121 --> 00:14:50.730
and to be able to
reason around it.

00:14:50.731 --> 00:14:52.700
In office, it turns out we're

00:14:52.701 --> 00:14:55.170
also starting to now
bring that technology

00:14:55.171 --> 00:14:56.875
and that knowledge infusion

00:14:56.876 --> 00:15:00.510
into the experiences
you all know like Word.

00:15:00.511 --> 00:15:03.810
In this case, imagine you're
writing some article,

00:15:03.811 --> 00:15:06.235
you're writing a paper
and you want to know,

00:15:06.236 --> 00:15:08.180
hey, I got to be inspired

00:15:08.181 --> 00:15:10.530
or tell me a little bit of
contextual information.

00:15:10.531 --> 00:15:12.710
In this case, since we're

00:15:12.711 --> 00:15:15.330
systematically bringing
what's available on the web,

00:15:15.331 --> 00:15:16.970
from the knowledge graphs,

00:15:16.971 --> 00:15:20.540
from internal to the company
to now be contextually

00:15:20.541 --> 00:15:22.315
relevant to the things that's

00:15:22.316 --> 00:15:24.520
happening in your work space,

00:15:24.521 --> 00:15:26.280
in the thing that you're
currently working on.

00:15:26.281 --> 00:15:27.650
Again, it's a different way of

00:15:27.651 --> 00:15:29.720
bringing in
that connective tissue

00:15:29.721 --> 00:15:33.680
of contexts that we think
allows you to stay in flow.

00:15:33.681 --> 00:15:35.020
If we look at productivity,

00:15:35.021 --> 00:15:38.320
one way we defined productivity
is staying in the flow,

00:15:38.321 --> 00:15:40.700
where you are most
productive as long as you

00:15:40.701 --> 00:15:43.530
can and bringing
that contextual knowledge in

00:15:43.531 --> 00:15:46.795
a relevant integrate away to
anticipate that next step

00:15:46.796 --> 00:15:50.450
is in fact a hallmark of
good knowledge capabilities.

00:15:50.451 --> 00:15:54.420
In fact, it doesn't even stop
at the word or the flow.

00:15:54.421 --> 00:15:55.810
Imagine you're in Excel,

00:15:55.811 --> 00:15:57.985
you got lots of different ways of

00:15:57.986 --> 00:16:00.865
describing data and values and

00:16:00.866 --> 00:16:02.940
the fact that there's
information there are

00:16:02.941 --> 00:16:05.995
referenced that may be valuable
for you to contextualize.

00:16:05.996 --> 00:16:07.535
So, in this case for example,

00:16:07.536 --> 00:16:10.530
you can imagine that let's
say you have the word United,

00:16:10.531 --> 00:16:12.440
but appears in
different contexts.

00:16:12.441 --> 00:16:14.465
This is just to
illustrate the complexity

00:16:14.466 --> 00:16:17.565
and the richness of the language
but also the ambiguity.

00:16:17.566 --> 00:16:19.970
So, in this case, United in

00:16:19.971 --> 00:16:22.985
the last context is in
fact a bunch of movies.

00:16:22.986 --> 00:16:25.250
But we wouldn't know
that unless we actually

00:16:25.251 --> 00:16:28.200
understood the other elements
be able to conflate.

00:16:28.201 --> 00:16:31.615
Likewise, in other contexts
it could be an airline,

00:16:31.616 --> 00:16:33.645
it could be companies,

00:16:33.646 --> 00:16:36.075
it could be European
football clubs,

00:16:36.076 --> 00:16:38.480
I mean it could be
many different ways.

00:16:38.481 --> 00:16:40.530
But again context matters and

00:16:40.531 --> 00:16:43.585
the ability to model
that is in fact rich.

00:16:43.586 --> 00:16:45.400
So, we're only
beginning to scratch

00:16:45.401 --> 00:16:48.530
the surface of bringing
information and

00:16:48.531 --> 00:16:51.055
knowledge in the context of user

00:16:51.056 --> 00:16:54.700
need in context or through
explicit queries and intent.

00:16:54.701 --> 00:16:56.265
But even beyond this,

00:16:56.266 --> 00:16:57.660
the one thing that
we've discovered

00:16:57.661 --> 00:16:58.805
as we start working on

00:16:58.806 --> 00:17:02.680
agents and assistance and
bots is that, whereas,

00:17:02.681 --> 00:17:04.345
knowledge may be considered to

00:17:04.346 --> 00:17:06.130
be valuable but it's
still nice to have,

00:17:06.131 --> 00:17:08.230
you can still get your work
done with temporal links,

00:17:08.231 --> 00:17:10.520
you can still get
your Word document

00:17:10.521 --> 00:17:14.045
done without being inspired
by contextual search.

00:17:14.046 --> 00:17:15.780
But in the case of conversations,

00:17:15.781 --> 00:17:17.930
especially conversations that go

00:17:17.931 --> 00:17:20.795
multi-turn, you need knowledge.

00:17:20.796 --> 00:17:23.140
The reason is the context and

00:17:23.141 --> 00:17:24.595
the information interactions that

00:17:24.596 --> 00:17:25.930
you have one turn needs to be

00:17:25.931 --> 00:17:28.030
passed and transferred to

00:17:28.031 --> 00:17:29.440
the next one so that
you can start to

00:17:29.441 --> 00:17:31.790
reason in that fluidness

00:17:31.791 --> 00:17:34.505
and that sharing of
contexts across turns,

00:17:34.506 --> 00:17:37.380
where the turns and the actions
taken on each turn,

00:17:37.381 --> 00:17:39.255
may be from different vendors,

00:17:39.256 --> 00:17:42.030
different applications and
different knowledge bases,

00:17:42.031 --> 00:17:44.835
is in fact one of
the hallmark challenges

00:17:44.836 --> 00:17:46.660
and opportunities in
conversation design.

00:17:46.661 --> 00:17:48.865
So, in this case,
imagine that you are now

00:17:48.866 --> 00:17:51.440
going through this flow.

00:17:51.441 --> 00:17:53.030
In fact, this is inspired by

00:17:53.031 --> 00:17:55.310
our semantic machines
acquisition.

00:17:55.311 --> 00:17:56.715
We're very excited to get

00:17:56.716 --> 00:17:58.835
Dan Klein and Percy to
be part of our family,

00:17:58.836 --> 00:18:00.545
but in this case,
imagine you say,

00:18:00.546 --> 00:18:01.910
"Hey, I want to go
to New York two days

00:18:01.911 --> 00:18:03.440
before thanks giving,

00:18:03.441 --> 00:18:05.835
what is two days
before thanks giving?

00:18:05.836 --> 00:18:07.240
What does it mean on New York?

00:18:07.241 --> 00:18:08.455
Where are the airports?

00:18:08.456 --> 00:18:10.505
How do I understand it?

00:18:10.506 --> 00:18:11.670
How do I reflected?

00:18:11.671 --> 00:18:13.805
How do I understand the
fastest elaboration?"

00:18:13.806 --> 00:18:16.005
These are all things that
you would say, yeah,

00:18:16.006 --> 00:18:18.030
it actually requires
you to orchestrate

00:18:18.031 --> 00:18:21.895
across many backend
systems in APIs.

00:18:21.896 --> 00:18:24.860
Each one has an ontology in

00:18:24.861 --> 00:18:28.400
some sense of the values
of the capabilities.

00:18:28.401 --> 00:18:30.275
So, in this case,
it's really about

00:18:30.276 --> 00:18:32.275
this ability to use knowledge to

00:18:32.276 --> 00:18:35.690
connect the dots across turns to

00:18:35.691 --> 00:18:37.730
be able to reason
and contextualize

00:18:37.731 --> 00:18:39.455
and to guide that discussion.

00:18:39.456 --> 00:18:41.325
So, in this case, take travel in

00:18:41.326 --> 00:18:43.720
New York to be able
to now recognize that

00:18:43.721 --> 00:18:45.900
nearby airports of New York are

00:18:45.901 --> 00:18:48.180
JFK and this certain location.

00:18:48.181 --> 00:18:50.240
Likewise you can
now imagine each of

00:18:50.241 --> 00:18:52.720
the APIs and each of
the systems having

00:18:52.721 --> 00:18:55.364
its own data and we need
to learn the association

00:18:55.365 --> 00:18:58.550
and do dynamic conflation
across these.

00:18:58.551 --> 00:19:03.180
Now, with all of the things
said, with knowledge,

00:19:03.181 --> 00:19:07.155
there are many things you
can do to start to now bring

00:19:07.156 --> 00:19:11.455
that knowledge in the context
of interactions and flows.

00:19:11.456 --> 00:19:13.915
But how do we bring this to life?

00:19:13.916 --> 00:19:18.905
This is a rich area of
research and product efforts.

00:19:18.906 --> 00:19:21.375
I'm not going to go through

00:19:21.376 --> 00:19:22.840
the details on this because

00:19:22.841 --> 00:19:24.390
I think you're all world experts.

00:19:24.391 --> 00:19:25.790
But I do want to
share a little bit

00:19:25.791 --> 00:19:28.090
of how we're looking at

00:19:28.091 --> 00:19:32.525
the dimensions of what
knowledge systems, the quality.

00:19:32.526 --> 00:19:34.930
What does that mean
and also some of

00:19:34.931 --> 00:19:37.490
the challenges that
we have that we

00:19:37.491 --> 00:19:40.670
think are really pushing us
to the limit but certainly an

00:19:40.671 --> 00:19:42.315
area that we'd like to invite

00:19:42.316 --> 00:19:44.240
your creativity and
your collaboration.

00:19:44.241 --> 00:19:46.630
So, in this case, to bring
knowledge systems to live,

00:19:46.631 --> 00:19:48.745
we start with the
fact that data can

00:19:48.746 --> 00:19:51.735
be chaotic and come from
structured and unstructured.

00:19:51.736 --> 00:19:53.520
Lots of effort across

00:19:53.521 --> 00:19:55.760
different pieces but
bringing that together,

00:19:55.761 --> 00:19:58.500
in some coherent knowledge
production process

00:19:58.501 --> 00:20:00.635
to be something where is fresh,

00:20:00.636 --> 00:20:02.315
highly structured, semantically

00:20:02.316 --> 00:20:03.655
understandable,
that's a challenge.

00:20:03.656 --> 00:20:05.880
That's the data chaos to

00:20:05.881 --> 00:20:08.175
the structured semantics flow.

00:20:08.176 --> 00:20:09.960
There are different approaches.

00:20:09.961 --> 00:20:15.060
Not that one approach is
better but in fact over time,

00:20:15.061 --> 00:20:17.370
a number of these
will work in concert.

00:20:17.371 --> 00:20:20.430
Starting with people, Wikipedia,

00:20:20.431 --> 00:20:22.670
DBpedia like there are
certain efforts that

00:20:22.671 --> 00:20:25.380
really do require
the domain experts to start

00:20:25.381 --> 00:20:28.565
capturing that knowledge in
some descendible way and to

00:20:28.566 --> 00:20:31.890
be able to now create an
incentive that keeps it fresh.

00:20:31.891 --> 00:20:33.400
Cool Wikipedia is
the great example

00:20:33.401 --> 00:20:36.280
almost every search engine
looks at Wikipedia and say,

00:20:36.281 --> 00:20:38.570
that's great, let's use that
to seed our understanding.

00:20:38.571 --> 00:20:41.295
Because that's probably
the best articulation

00:20:41.296 --> 00:20:45.035
of the basic shareable knowledge
that people interact.

00:20:45.036 --> 00:20:46.415
That's one of the facets

00:20:46.416 --> 00:20:47.835
that I think it's
important for knowledge.

00:20:47.836 --> 00:20:51.120
It's not just important
for systems to understand.

00:20:51.121 --> 00:20:52.530
It is something that needs to be

00:20:52.531 --> 00:20:55.530
understandable and
explainable to people.

00:20:55.531 --> 00:20:59.515
But beyond people, at some point,

00:20:59.516 --> 00:21:01.845
you're going to run out of
steam because at some point,

00:21:01.846 --> 00:21:03.605
either the willingness
or the capacity of

00:21:03.606 --> 00:21:05.665
people are going to hit a limit.

00:21:05.666 --> 00:21:08.205
So, this is where systems
start to come in.

00:21:08.206 --> 00:21:11.750
This theme of systems for
AI and AI for systems,

00:21:11.751 --> 00:21:13.915
is in fact one of
the hallmarks where I think it

00:21:13.916 --> 00:21:16.580
applies beautifully
to knowledge system.

00:21:16.581 --> 00:21:19.150
In this case, we can
imagine implicit modeling.

00:21:19.151 --> 00:21:22.210
We talked about deep machine
reading comprehension.

00:21:22.211 --> 00:21:24.885
We're still at the early stages
of it but again,

00:21:24.886 --> 00:21:26.670
this is a case where
we're now trying

00:21:26.671 --> 00:21:28.770
to understand the shape,

00:21:28.771 --> 00:21:29.960
the language, shape of

00:21:29.961 --> 00:21:32.665
information and the
shape of the retrieval.

00:21:32.666 --> 00:21:34.150
Lots of efforts on that.

00:21:34.151 --> 00:21:35.730
But there's also knowledge

00:21:35.731 --> 00:21:37.985
representations
that are explicit.

00:21:37.986 --> 00:21:40.200
These are the triplets,
these are RDFs,

00:21:40.201 --> 00:21:42.180
these are the different
graph structures.

00:21:42.181 --> 00:21:44.390
There, I would say we have a lots

00:21:44.391 --> 00:21:47.935
of research and lots
of production systems,

00:21:47.936 --> 00:21:52.040
being Google, Facebook, LinkedIn,

00:21:52.041 --> 00:21:53.605
there are all the
systems that are

00:21:53.606 --> 00:21:55.820
creating these knowledge
representations.

00:21:55.821 --> 00:21:58.050
Some which are proprietary,
some of which are public.

00:21:58.051 --> 00:22:01.320
In fact, a lot of
research systems psych

00:22:01.321 --> 00:22:02.660
from the early days all the

00:22:02.661 --> 00:22:05.115
way to the research systems
that exist today.

00:22:05.116 --> 00:22:06.655
This is an active area.

00:22:06.656 --> 00:22:09.185
Now, what I want to do is just

00:22:09.186 --> 00:22:11.860
talk a little bit about
regardless of the approach,

00:22:11.861 --> 00:22:14.060
there are different dimensions

00:22:14.061 --> 00:22:17.120
that we evaluate and
assess knowledge.

00:22:17.121 --> 00:22:19.520
Is a knowledge system correct?

00:22:19.521 --> 00:22:21.475
What's the degree of correctness?

00:22:21.476 --> 00:22:24.690
What's the degree of freshness?
What's their coverage?

00:22:24.691 --> 00:22:27.320
There's a standard but when
you start looking at it,

00:22:27.321 --> 00:22:31.130
they work against each other
when you hit extreme scale.

00:22:31.131 --> 00:22:33.650
In fact, that's where
we end up which is,

00:22:33.651 --> 00:22:36.780
it all sounds good for
one million documents,

00:22:36.781 --> 00:22:38.490
it sounds good for 10 million.

00:22:38.491 --> 00:22:41.390
It works really hard if
you have hundreds of

00:22:41.391 --> 00:22:44.650
billion and that's
the chaotic Web.

00:22:44.651 --> 00:22:46.535
It's not just chaotic web,

00:22:46.536 --> 00:22:52.165
it's chaotic enterprise systems
and real-life situations.

00:22:52.166 --> 00:22:55.680
With that, let me just
give some examples.

00:22:55.681 --> 00:22:57.010
In the case of correctness,

00:22:57.011 --> 00:22:58.845
precision really does matter.

00:22:58.846 --> 00:23:01.045
Because once you
create that knowledge,

00:23:01.046 --> 00:23:02.945
you have to stand by the quality.

00:23:02.946 --> 00:23:04.650
If something is wrong,
you can't just point to

00:23:04.651 --> 00:23:06.660
the source and say, I don't know.

00:23:06.661 --> 00:23:08.680
I think I extracted it right.

00:23:08.681 --> 00:23:11.485
This is fake news. It's
fake knowledge graph.

00:23:11.486 --> 00:23:13.665
While you got to
look at authority.

00:23:13.666 --> 00:23:14.870
You got to look at authority.

00:23:14.871 --> 00:23:16.580
You got to look at the synthesis.

00:23:16.581 --> 00:23:18.235
How do I look at voting?

00:23:18.236 --> 00:23:20.555
If I don't have an authority,
how do I judge?

00:23:20.556 --> 00:23:21.930
How do I get user feedback?

00:23:21.931 --> 00:23:24.420
That's a challenge
especially when you have

00:23:24.421 --> 00:23:29.050
an orchestrated multi-party
sources of information.

00:23:29.051 --> 00:23:32.365
Freshness, speed matters,
things are constantly changing.

00:23:32.366 --> 00:23:34.965
In many cases we don't
even know what changed,

00:23:34.966 --> 00:23:36.640
not even to mention
the ability to

00:23:36.641 --> 00:23:38.460
propagate that update
through the system in

00:23:38.461 --> 00:23:40.580
a way where we understand that

00:23:40.581 --> 00:23:43.050
some of the updates may
in fact be incorrect.

00:23:43.051 --> 00:23:45.385
So, you can actually
start propagating

00:23:45.386 --> 00:23:48.030
lots of challenges
with one mistake.

00:23:48.031 --> 00:23:50.160
You can ripple and destroy pretty

00:23:50.161 --> 00:23:52.580
much everything and that's
the lesson we have.

00:23:52.581 --> 00:23:55.260
In coverage, right size
really does matter,

00:23:55.261 --> 00:23:56.600
at some point they'll say great,

00:23:56.601 --> 00:23:58.575
this all sounds good
but is it complete,

00:23:58.576 --> 00:24:00.180
