00:27:09.411 --> 00:27:11.660
So, let's start with
the inherent complexity

00:27:11.661 --> 00:27:13.590
just to motivate
this a little bit.

00:27:13.591 --> 00:27:17.185
Working Web search is beautiful.

00:27:17.186 --> 00:27:21.710
It's chaotic, nobody has
control over anything and

00:27:21.711 --> 00:27:27.395
things completely changed
at some break neck pace.

00:27:27.396 --> 00:27:29.800
But there are three dimensions
that really put

00:27:29.801 --> 00:27:32.030
pressure on the things we do.

00:27:32.031 --> 00:27:35.595
One is just the logic
which is hey,

00:27:35.596 --> 00:27:38.080
lots of detailed information

00:27:38.081 --> 00:27:40.755
describing different ontologies
across different sites,

00:27:40.756 --> 00:27:43.420
at what point does it
make sense to generalize,

00:27:43.421 --> 00:27:45.235
at what point does it become

00:27:45.236 --> 00:27:47.830
common patterns or
across domains?

00:27:47.831 --> 00:27:52.160
How do I now enlist
domain experts and how do I now

00:27:52.161 --> 00:27:54.810
recognize that domain experts
don't exist only in

00:27:54.811 --> 00:27:56.010
one company that in fact

00:27:56.011 --> 00:27:57.550
it's decentralized
and distributed?

00:27:57.551 --> 00:27:59.980
So, being able to tap
into that and be able to

00:27:59.981 --> 00:28:02.550
reason on both the domain

00:28:02.551 --> 00:28:04.410
specific but also
the domain general,

00:28:04.411 --> 00:28:05.905
these are the common sense.

00:28:05.906 --> 00:28:08.150
These are the basic
things on units,

00:28:08.151 --> 00:28:11.030
on basic understanding of
distance but there are

00:28:11.031 --> 00:28:12.180
lots of things that I think

00:28:12.181 --> 00:28:14.444
are shareable and fundamental.

00:28:14.445 --> 00:28:16.930
On the time dimension
everything changes,

00:28:16.931 --> 00:28:20.350
which exist that nobody tells
us that they are changing.

00:28:20.351 --> 00:28:23.030
So, even coming up with
both the ability to

00:28:23.031 --> 00:28:27.650
detect the status
updates but also be

00:28:27.651 --> 00:28:28.880
able to see whether
you can create

00:28:28.881 --> 00:28:31.040
even the incentives where
they are willing to tell

00:28:31.041 --> 00:28:33.160
you that things are changing and

00:28:33.161 --> 00:28:35.625
so to look at systems
or system integrations.

00:28:35.626 --> 00:28:38.940
In the space you can imagine
that the category and

00:28:38.941 --> 00:28:40.080
the domain and the scope

00:28:40.081 --> 00:28:42.440
continues to expand
across domains,

00:28:42.441 --> 00:28:44.960
across facets, across entity.

00:28:44.961 --> 00:28:46.985
So, in Bing,

00:28:46.986 --> 00:28:49.420
I'd say that there are
a couple of pivotal points in

00:28:49.421 --> 00:28:51.670
which we've shifted that

00:28:51.671 --> 00:28:54.300
really grew our horsepower
to tackle some of these.

00:28:54.301 --> 00:28:56.965
I'll list three of
them. The first one is

00:28:56.966 --> 00:28:59.340
a shift from
batch-based conflation

00:28:59.341 --> 00:29:00.965
to a streaming-based conflation.

00:29:00.966 --> 00:29:02.470
That's a fundamental shift.

00:29:02.471 --> 00:29:04.570
Imagine it's no longer that hey,

00:29:04.571 --> 00:29:08.150
on Monday of every week you
take all the data sources,

00:29:08.151 --> 00:29:11.075
you do a big job and you

00:29:11.076 --> 00:29:15.035
publish a big blob of
a graph, is it correct?

00:29:15.036 --> 00:29:18.100
I hope so but it takes time,

00:29:18.101 --> 00:29:21.560
it's used to be
a couple of weeks.

00:29:21.561 --> 00:29:23.930
But the Web doesn't
work like that,

00:29:23.931 --> 00:29:27.220
it's it's not a discretized
sequence events.

00:29:27.221 --> 00:29:28.360
So, we shifted into

00:29:28.361 --> 00:29:31.015
a streaming-based system
which changes everything,

00:29:31.016 --> 00:29:33.205
the notion of having
an incremental base,

00:29:33.206 --> 00:29:34.310
the ability to start looking at

00:29:34.311 --> 00:29:35.570
updates in a different way,

00:29:35.571 --> 00:29:37.990
they are ready to now look at

00:29:37.991 --> 00:29:40.845
the incremental conflation
and evolution

00:29:40.846 --> 00:29:44.025
and even reason about
correctness in a different way.

00:29:44.026 --> 00:29:47.070
The second shift we have
is to start to look

00:29:47.071 --> 00:29:50.670
at going from the head
to the tail and

00:29:50.671 --> 00:29:52.510
that requires us to

00:29:52.511 --> 00:29:55.590
dramatically scale
our ability to both manage

00:29:55.591 --> 00:29:57.760
the ontology but also
start to go into

00:29:57.761 --> 00:30:01.620
deeper site in domain
understanding in an automated way.

00:30:01.621 --> 00:30:04.050
Again, that's an area where
we're pushing more and

00:30:04.051 --> 00:30:06.755
more but clearly lots
more to be done.

00:30:06.756 --> 00:30:08.850
I think the last one
that I think it's

00:30:08.851 --> 00:30:11.365
notable is our view
of correctness.

00:30:11.366 --> 00:30:13.960
Correctness, it's not like
everything out there is

00:30:13.961 --> 00:30:15.220
correct or in fact there

00:30:15.221 --> 00:30:16.670
are different shades
of correctness,

00:30:16.671 --> 00:30:18.620
there are different
competence factors

00:30:18.621 --> 00:30:21.575
and yet nobody is there to
be the ultimate arbiter.

00:30:21.576 --> 00:30:22.970
How do we deal with that?

00:30:22.971 --> 00:30:26.100
How do we now make sure that
inputs and changes that are

00:30:26.101 --> 00:30:29.775
proposed are hypothesis that
allows us to reason score,

00:30:29.776 --> 00:30:31.975
understand the
likelihood of churn

00:30:31.976 --> 00:30:34.340
before it goes into
the rest of the system,

00:30:34.341 --> 00:30:35.940
may be able to now
get that feedback?

00:30:35.941 --> 00:30:38.030
So, these are
just examples in which

00:30:38.031 --> 00:30:40.410
the current system continuously

00:30:40.411 --> 00:30:42.365
evolving that we like to say

00:30:42.366 --> 00:30:45.340
the colleague Yushin Gale
who's in the audience,

00:30:45.341 --> 00:30:47.170
who's running
this authority would

00:30:47.171 --> 00:30:49.195
say that knowledge is
always the life system,

00:30:49.196 --> 00:30:50.735
it's a live system.

00:30:50.736 --> 00:30:52.965
It's not like you build
it and it's done,

00:30:52.966 --> 00:30:55.110
it's a constant,
constant evolution.

00:30:55.111 --> 00:30:57.530
So, lots of challenges
that you can imagine

00:30:57.531 --> 00:31:00.300
both systems and
algorithmic advances

00:31:00.301 --> 00:31:02.220
that allows us to now
tackle some of these,

00:31:02.221 --> 00:31:04.230
so that they can continue to grow

00:31:04.231 --> 00:31:06.820
and evolve with
the complexity of the Web.

00:31:06.821 --> 00:31:10.800
The second area is something
we've talked about already,

00:31:10.801 --> 00:31:12.360
which is knowledge can be

00:31:12.361 --> 00:31:15.390
represented explicitly
or implicitly and

00:31:15.391 --> 00:31:16.950
we've seen great advances and

00:31:16.951 --> 00:31:20.780
great promise in the neural
modeling of information.

00:31:20.781 --> 00:31:22.980
We've also seen the advances

00:31:22.981 --> 00:31:24.780
on symbolic but there
are pros and cons.

00:31:24.781 --> 00:31:28.795
At some point the
discretized representation

00:31:28.796 --> 00:31:31.485
is probably too big and too

00:31:31.486 --> 00:31:35.390
hard to manage in
the context of now

00:31:35.391 --> 00:31:39.440
joining against their intent
or contexts and vice versa.

00:31:39.441 --> 00:31:43.410
So, their benefits are both.
Their benefits are both.

00:31:43.411 --> 00:31:45.130
One is understandable to

00:31:45.131 --> 00:31:47.470
humans but really
computationally not

00:31:47.471 --> 00:31:50.290
efficient when you start
looking at the mirror

00:31:50.291 --> 00:31:53.520
add up understanding that
relatedness and all that stuff,

00:31:53.521 --> 00:31:55.180
and yet our neural it's efficient

00:31:55.181 --> 00:31:57.550
but sometimes you're not
quite sure what's happening.

00:31:57.551 --> 00:31:59.515
So, we've taken some efforts,

00:31:59.516 --> 00:32:01.560
I just list out
one example but this

00:32:01.561 --> 00:32:03.530
is clearly an active area
of research that we

00:32:03.531 --> 00:32:05.080
hope that we'll see

00:32:05.081 --> 00:32:08.140
some good advances and
breakthrough because were seeing

00:32:08.141 --> 00:32:09.620
the need to have actually

00:32:09.621 --> 00:32:12.955
both techniques applied
systematically.

00:32:12.956 --> 00:32:15.030
One example is let's
say you do have

00:32:15.031 --> 00:32:17.570
a neural system that
allows you to model

00:32:17.571 --> 00:32:19.965
against some embedding space

00:32:19.966 --> 00:32:21.190
and you have
a knowledge graph and

00:32:21.191 --> 00:32:23.000
the question is how do I now use

00:32:23.001 --> 00:32:25.565
a knowledge graph to
bootstrap by understanding?

00:32:25.566 --> 00:32:28.460
The way you do that is in
order to do this mapping,

00:32:28.461 --> 00:32:32.145
we first understand
the hypothesis

00:32:32.146 --> 00:32:34.790
that are available in terms

00:32:34.791 --> 00:32:37.310
of the questions and answers
in the knowledge graph.

00:32:37.311 --> 00:32:39.720
We apply that through
the system so it

00:32:39.721 --> 00:32:42.860
learns and maps it against
an embedding space.

00:32:42.861 --> 00:32:44.850
Oh sorry, I went too fast

00:32:44.851 --> 00:32:46.670
maps it against
an embedded space.

00:32:46.671 --> 00:32:48.330
So, overtime you can imagine that

00:32:48.331 --> 00:32:50.695
through techniques
like this or similar,

00:32:50.696 --> 00:32:52.180
we can hopefully start to

00:32:52.181 --> 00:32:56.090
now bootstrap and connect and
hopefully even do this in

00:32:56.091 --> 00:32:57.540
a much more integrated
way but this is

00:32:57.541 --> 00:32:59.520
an active area of
research that I encourage

00:32:59.521 --> 00:33:03.460
all of you to look at and
see what we can do together.

00:33:03.461 --> 00:33:05.875
Then on the enterprise,

00:33:05.876 --> 00:33:09.080
going back again on
this enthusiasm that

00:33:09.081 --> 00:33:11.790
people have around
enterprises and

00:33:11.791 --> 00:33:13.975
their knowledge but lots of

00:33:13.976 --> 00:33:19.015
unstructured information in
people's communications,

00:33:19.016 --> 00:33:20.655
in the documents people write.

00:33:20.656 --> 00:33:22.265
People don't writing structured

